abr-au is an unofficial, independent client. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed or approved by the Australian Business Register, the Australian
Taxation Office or the Commonwealth of Australia.

This software contains no Australian Business Register data. It reads data
that the user downloads separately:

* ABN Lookup Bulk Extract — Australian Business Register, published on
  data.gov.au (https://data.gov.au/data/dataset/abn-bulk-extract) under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia licence
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/au/). Anyone redistributing an
  index built from it, or outputs derived from it, must give attribution, for
  example: "Contains ABN Lookup data from the Australian Business Register
  (ABN Bulk Extract, data.gov.au), licensed under CC BY 3.0 AU."

* ABN Lookup web services (optional) — live data from abr.business.gov.au,
  used under the ABN Lookup Web Services Agreement that each user accepts
  when registering for their own GUID
  (https://abr.business.gov.au/Tools/WebServicesAgreement). No GUID is
  included, and web-service responses are not cached or stored.

The ABN and ACN check-digit algorithms are the published ATO and ASIC rules.
The name-normalisation rule derives from DeepCivic's grants/procurement
analysis, and the bulk-extract field projection from the Womblex `ingest-abn`
register ingest (both DeepCivic projects).
